stickanimationengine4000-by-faemiyah for Debian
-----------------------------------------------

This is the standard version of the 4k intro, not the size-optimized "party"
version: configure defines SAE4_GNU_LD, so the program is linked normally
against SDL2, freeglut, GLU and OpenGL instead of loading them with dlopen.
The binaries shipped upstream in rel/ are not installed.

Changes made by the Debian patches:
 - port from SDL 1.2 to SDL2, resizable window that keeps the 16:9 ratio;
 - F toggles fullscreen, Esc, Q or the close button quit;
 - V-Sync enabled, and the time of the intro starts with the music: the
   soundtrack is synthesised after SDL is initialised, which made the
   picture run ahead of the music on slow machines;
 - the executable is no longer stripped at link time (-s), dh_strip does it.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

